{% extends 'site/guideBase.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}
    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">World Map</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>
                The world map is the main interface of the game. It is an interactive hex-based map that you can zoom and pan to explore.
                The map size depends on which world you are playing in.
            </p>
            <p>
                Your resources and income are displayed at the top of the screen. Active fleets are shown on the map as they travel between regions.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Terrain Types</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>The world is made up of different terrain types. Terrain affects what you can build:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Grassland</b> &mdash; Standard land region.</li>
                <li><b>Forest</b> &mdash; Standard land region.</li>
                <li><b>Hills</b> &mdash; Standard land region.</li>
                <li><b>Mountain</b> &mdash; Standard land region.</li>
                <li><b>Sand</b> &mdash; Standard land region.</li>
                <li><b>Shallow Water</b> &mdash; Water region.</li>
                <li><b>Water</b> &mdash; Water region.</li>
                <li><b>Deep Water</b> &mdash; Water region.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                A region is considered <b>coastal</b> if it is a land region that shares a border with a water region.
                Harbors can only be built on coastal regions, and ships can only attack water and coastal regions.
            </p>
            <p>
                Water regions can't be bought. Send ships to open sea next to one of your regions and occupy it when they arrive.
                You hold a water region only while you have units, a Sea Mine or a Sea Mine under construction on it; once the
                last units leave or are destroyed it becomes open sea again. Sea Mines are the only thing you can build on water.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <br/>

    <div class="uw-card">
        <div class="uw-card-header">Interacting with the Map</div>
        <div class="uw-card-body">
            <p>Click on a hex tile to interact with it. What you can do depends on who owns the region:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <b>Your region:</b> Opens the region panel where you can view your buildings and units,
                    start <a href="{{ url('Guide/Construction') }}">construction</a>, and <a href="{{ url('Guide/Fleet') }}">send units</a> to other regions.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Enemy region:</b> Shows <a href="{{ url('Guide/Attack') }}">attack</a> options if you have units within range.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <b>Unowned region:</b> You can buy this land region to expand your empire. The cost increases with each region you already own. Open sea can only be claimed with ships.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
